      "id": "nm000275",
      "name": "Multi-channel EEG recordings during a sustained-attention driving task",
      "description": "This dataset provides BIDS-EEG formatted raw recordings from 27 healthy adults performing a sustained-attention driving task in a virtual-reality driving simulator on a motion platform. It comprises 62 sessions (~82 hours) of 32-channel EEG at 500 Hz plus a vehicle lateral-position channel. Events mark randomly induced lane-departure onsets and the participants' steering responses, allowing study of reaction time as an index of fatigue and drowsiness.",
